 security information associated with a protected object. Security descriptors include information about who owns the object, who can access it and in what way, and what types of access are audited.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109159">security descriptor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411454">descriptor de seguretat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11565_210476_364128"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphic that represents a rating that is indicated visually by stars (e.g. ★★★) where the higher number of stars indicates the highest rating.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210476">star rating</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="364128">Valoració amb estrelles</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11567_216558_1550692"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To arrange to receive a product or use a service regularly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="216558">subscribe</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1550692">subscriure</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11568_397198_410986"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mailbox server that is installed in a Windows failover cluster. A clustered mailbox server is used in both cluster continuous replication (CCR) and single copy cluster (SCC) configurations. A clustered mailbox server was called an Exchange Virtual Server in previous versions of Exchange Server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397198">clustered mailbox server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="410986">servidor de bústies de correu en clúster</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11576_358360_362924"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of components and services that enable voice, fax, and email messages to be stored in a user's single mailbox. Users can also access their Microsoft Exchange Server 2007 mailbox from a telephone or a computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358360">Unified Messaging server role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="362924">Funció del servidor de missatgeria unificada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1160_30078_2715585"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In computers, the linking of two or more entities so that they are dependent upon one another for operation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="30078">chaining</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2715585">encadenament</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11602_502823_514663"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A UI element that sends an instant message to the selected person inviting them to join the current conversation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="502823">Invite Someone</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="514663">Invita algú</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11608_75547_1143715"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character that separates items in a list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="75547">list separator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1143715">separador de llista</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfS