">The top level of a business hierarchy.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="182655">organization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546188">organització</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12311_374324_2095202"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type that is automatically updated every time a row is inserted or updated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="374324">timestamp</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095202">data i hora</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12313_56589_1555367"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An independent section on a webpage. Each frame is actually a separate webpage and can have its own scrollbars.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="56589">frame</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1555367">marc</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12314_1230148_1963698"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application that consolidates a user's voice mail, fax, and email into one mailbox, so that the user only needs to check a single location for messages, regardless of type. The email server is used as the platform for all types of messages, making it unnecessary to maintain separate voice mail and email infrastructures.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1230148">UM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1963698">UM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12314_1230148_411888"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application that consolidates a user's voice mail, fax, and email into one mailbox, so that the user only needs to check a single location for messages, regardless of type. The email server is used as the platform for all types of messages, making it unnecessary to maintain separate voice mail and email infrastructures.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1230148">UM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411888">missatgeria unificada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12314_234514_1963698"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An application that consolidate