</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1555447">dispositiu d'entrada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14196_185627_512268"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An item the user can select in the Options dialog box, Phones tab, from the "Select the default device for calling phone numbers" drop-down list. When the user selects Computer as the default device for calling phone numbers, Communicator uses the Voice Over Internet Protocol (VOIP) connection for making a call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="185627">Computer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="512268">ordinador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14199_12503_1963179"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A non-validated user who is not recognized by the server, and who can only access published folders and address lists.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="12503">anonymous user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1963179">usuari anònim</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14200_117651_1550696"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One character (or more) that is slightly higher than other text on a line, such as a footnote reference mark.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="117651">superscript</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1550696">superíndex</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14205_397185_411298"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The X.400 term for a messaging system, which is a product that enables electronic communication over a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397185">message transfer system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411298">MTS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14205_397185_411299"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The X.400 term for a messaging system, which is a product that enables electronic communication over a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397185">message transfer system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411299">sistema de transferència de missatges</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14205_397186_411298"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The X.400 term for a messaging system, which is a product that enables electronic communication over a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397186">MTS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411298">MTS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14205_397186_411299"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The X.400 term for a messaging system, which is a product that enables electronic communication over a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397186">MTS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411299">sistema de transferència de missatges</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1421_145137_2785752"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A network type that a computer is connected to that automatically sets the appropriate firewall settings for the location.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145137">network location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2785752">ubicació de la xarxa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14210_2307008_2768099"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The act of reducing the probability and/or impact of a risk to an acceptable level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2307008">mitigation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2768099">mitigació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14210_252102_2768099"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The act of reducing the probability and/or impact of a risk to an acceptable level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="252102">risk mitigation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2768099">mitigació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14211_213519_2638569"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An order for a SKU that is currently not available for delivery.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="213519">pre-order</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2638569">compra per endavant</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14212_338602_1821142"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The status message displayed for the current network when a user changes the network selection to something other than the network of the main provider.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="338602">Home service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1821142">Trucada local</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14216_397178_411287"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of recipients that are created to expedite the mass emailing of messages and other information. When email is sent to a mail-enabled universal distribution group, all members of that list receive a copy of the message. Mail-enabled universal distribution groups cannot be used to assign permissions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397178">mail-enabled universal distribution group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411287">grup de distribució universal habilitat per a correu electrònic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14217_183928_364143"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A wizard that lets users select, configure, and import data from a data source into a Visio diagram.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="183928">Data Selector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="364143">Selector de dades</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14217_269319_364143"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A wizard that lets users select, configure, and import data from a data source into a Visio diagram.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269319">Data Selector Wizard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="364143">Selector de dades</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14219_310257_1143887"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows technology that protects OS resources (files, folders registry keys) and prevents applications and administrators from making changes to a computer's resources in an arbitrary way.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="310257">System Protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1143887">Protecció del sistema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14237_169312_2767884"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A database that functions as a backup of a primary database, receiving copies of every change to the primary database, and that can take over traffic if the primary database becomes unavailable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="169312">mirror database</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2767884">base de dades de reflex</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14238_2822_1545849"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A memory measurement unit that is equal to 1 million bytes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2822">MB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545849">MB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14238_2822_1545853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A memory measurement unit that is equal to 1 million bytes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2822">MB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545853">megabyte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14238_2823_1545849"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A memory measurement unit that is equal to 1 million bytes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2823">megabyte</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545849">MB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14238_2823_1545853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A memory measurement unit that is equal to 1 million bytes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2823">megabyte</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545853">megabyte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1424_61809_1555395"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To emphasize displayed characters, as by displaying them in reverse video (light on dark rather than dark on light, and vice versa) or against a colored background.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61809">highlight</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1555395">ressaltar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14241_45676_1547527"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In computing, a characteristic of data that is represented as binary digits (zeros and ones).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="45676">digital</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1547527">digital</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14244_115576_1979045"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To make a transmission appear to come from a user other than the user who performed the action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="115576">spoof</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1979045">suplantar la identitat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14244_115576_2776858"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To make a transmission appear to come from a user other than the user who performed the action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="115576">spoof</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2776858">suplantar electrònicament</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14244_115576_411543"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To make a transmission appear to come from a user other than the user who performed the action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="115576">spoof</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="411543">suplantar la identitat (spoof)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14245_294303_1276299"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A defined set of application access privileges. The security role assigned to a user determines which tasks the user can perform and which parts of the user interface the user can view. All users must be assigned at least one security role in order to access the system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294303">security role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1276299">funció de seguretat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14246_343618_1098259"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A diagramming capability that shows charts in three dimensions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="343618">3-D effect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098259">Efecte en 3D</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14256_72076_1555478"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To adjust horizontal spacing so that text is aligned evenly along both the left and right margins. Justifying text creates a smooth edge on both sides.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="72076">justify</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1555478">justificar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote ty