ed</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15809_499683_2714047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An entity that either starts or participates in an activity. Actors can be either initiators or targets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="499683">actor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2714047">actor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15814_140706_2094778"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A window that shows the design of these database objects - tables, queries, forms, reports, macros, and data access pages. In Design view, you can create new database objects and modify the design of existing ones.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="140706">Design view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094778">visualització Disseny</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15834_83662_1098344"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area of an application window that enables the user to navigate quickly to different parts of the program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="83662">navigation pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp