 products ordered should be sent.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="379960">bill-to address</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1276375">adreça de facturació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15885_446288_761221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A charge levied by a government on products, activities and employee or corporate income to finance government expenditure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="446288">tax</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="761221">impost</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15886_319136_1143930"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ‐ character, used to break a word between syllables at the end of a line or to separate the parts of a compound word.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="319136">HYPHEN</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1143930">guionet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15886_63086_1143930"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ‐ character, used to break a word between syllables at the end of a line or to separate the parts of a compound word.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="63086">hyphen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1143930">guionet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15888_62684_3041448"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A color model used in some graphics programs to define a color by three values: Hue, the color itself; Saturation, the purity of the color; and Value, the lightness or darkness of a color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="62684">HSV</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3041448">HSV</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15888_757192_3041448"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A color model used in some graphics programs to define a color by three values: Hue, the color itself; Saturation, the purity of the color; and Value, the lightness or darkness of a color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="757192">hue-saturation-value</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3041448">HSV</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15906_186205_1097929"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that must be enabled in Active Directory to run incremental import of profiles.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="186205">Server Side Incremental</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097929">Incremental de servidor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15926_234817_1143931"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An item on the Control Panel that provides user a comprehensive view over all roamed content, as well as ability to check on the synchronization progress of individual items.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="234817">Sync Center</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1143931">Centre de sincronització</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1593_108356_2145196"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descr