nd manipulate database objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651820">Data Access Objects</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094944">Data Access Objects</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17848_650208_2094954"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of creating two or more special copies (replicas) of an Access database. Replicas can be synchronized, changes made to data in one replica, or design changes made in the Design Master, are sent to other replicas.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650208">database replication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094954">replicació de base de dades</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17851_650211_2094957"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character that is used to separate the day, month, and year when date values are formatted. The characters are determined by system settings or by the Format function.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650211">date separator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094957">separador de dates</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17853_650213_2094960"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The default property setting of a control type. You customize a control type before you create two or more similar controls to avoid customizing each control individually.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650213">default control style</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094960">estil de control per defecte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17854_650214_2094774"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The font that a program uses by default to display text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650214">default font</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094774">tipus de lletra per defecte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17855_650215_2094961"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A property that you can set for a control so that each time a new control of that type is created, this property will have the same value.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650215">default property</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094961">propietat per defecte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17859_650219_1547519"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The amount of time between the scheduled start of a task and the time when work should actually begin on the task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650219">delay</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1547519">retard</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17861_650221_2094962"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The grid that you use to design a query or filter in query Design view or in the Advanced Filter/Sort window. For queries, this grid was formerly known as the QBE grid.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650221">design grid</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094962">quadrícula de disseny</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17863_650223_2094964"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The part of PivotTable view that contains detail and total fields.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650223">detail area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094964">àrea de detalls</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17865_650225_2094968"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Web site component that enables users to participate in topics of discussion by posting and replying to comments.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650225">discussion board</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094968">tauler de discussió</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17868_650228_2094971"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Characteristic of a number stored in twice the amount (two words; typically 8 bytes) of computer memory that is required for storing a less precise (single-precision) number. Commonly handled by a computer in floating-point form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650228">double-precision</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094971">precisió doble</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17877_650237_2094973"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of Access updating or repainting the screen while a macro is running.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650237">echo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094973">eco</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1789_114199_1821268"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To delay an item, such as a reminder, an alarm, or a recommendation, by a specified time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="114199">snooze</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1821268">ajornar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1794_264894_325443"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A template that addresses, from a Strategic Business Development perspective, the general activities that a company goes through to determine their business growth strategy. The roadmap includes understanding market position, evaluating trade-offs between mergers/acquisitions and internal development, evaluating M&amp;A candidates and placing valuation on target companies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="264894">Strategic Merger or Acquisition Evaluation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="325443">Avaluació d'adquisició o fusió estratègica</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1801_111907_1356004"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To make resources, such as folders, printers, files, photos, available to others.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="111907">share</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1356004">compartir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1808_180960_1273398"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">UI element consisting of a report toolbar and other navigation elements used to work with a report.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="180960">HTML Viewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1273398">Visualitzador d'HTML</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1809_149352_2094836"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control you place on a form or report to contain an unbound object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149352">unbound object frame</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094836">marc d'objecte independent</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1810_33647_2714375"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A system of symbols used to convert information from one form to another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="33647">code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2714375">codi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1813_52080_1355646"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A component you can use to view and manage event logs, gather information about hardware and software problems, and monitor security events. Event Viewer maintains logs about program, security, and system events.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="52080">Event Viewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1355646">visualitzador d'incidències</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1819_143381_2734551"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A path containing a document with hyperlinks that is used as the root of the hyperlinks in the document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="143381">hyperlink base</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2734551">base d'enllaços</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1820_76908_1545828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To execute a group of statements repeatedly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="76908">loop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545828">repetir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1821_4592_1537124"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To change a system or a data file to make it more current.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="4592">update</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1537124">actualitzar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1825_2484838_2042889"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual value plotted in a chart and represented together with other data points by bars, columns, lines, pie or doughnut slices, dots, and various other shapes called data markers. Data markers of the same color constitute a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2484838">series data point</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2042889">punt de dades</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1825_314089_2042889"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual value plotted in a chart and represented together with other data points by bars, columns, lines, pie or doughnut slices, dots, and various other shapes called data markers. Data markers of the same color constitute a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="314089">data point</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2042889">punt de dades</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1825_395743_2042889"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual value plotted in a chart and represented together with other data points by bars, columns, lines, pie or doughnut slices, dots, and various other shapes called data markers. Data markers of the same color constitute a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="395743">series point</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2042889">punt de dades</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1826_116591_1821278"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The hardware and software system used to retain data for subsequent retrieval.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116591">storage</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1821278">emmagatzematge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="183_122023_1550737"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A keyboard key that alternates between turning a particular operation, function, or mode on or off.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="122023">toggle key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1550737">tecla de commutació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1833_1165894_1724721"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Office Web application that provides secure access to email, personal calendar, group scheduling, and collaboration applications on Microsoft Exchange Server with only a Web browser.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1165894">Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1724721">Microsoft Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1833_1165894_1963603"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Office Web application that provides secure access to email, personal calendar, group scheduling, and collaboration applications on Microsoft Exchange Server with only a Web browser.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1165894">Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1963603">Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1833_1244832_1724721"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Office Web application that provides secure access to email, personal calendar, group scheduling, and collaboration applications on Microsoft Exchange Server with only a Web browser.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1244832">Microsoft Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1724721">Microsoft Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1833_1244832_1963603"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Office Web application that provides secure access to email, personal calendar, group scheduling, and collaboration applications on Microsoft Exchange Server with only a Web browser.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1244832">Microsoft Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1963603">Outlook Web App</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1835_144218_2734553"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A version of a program that has been localized for other markets and/or translated into other languages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144218">localized version</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2734553">versió localitzada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1839_127118_2094840"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A property that defines valid input values for a field or record in a table, or a control on a form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="127118">validation rule</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094840">norma de validació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1846_97122_1770079"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Able to be both read from and written to.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="97122">R/W</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770079">lectura/escriptura</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1846_97123_1770079"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Able to be both read from and written to.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="97123">read/write</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770079">lectura/escriptura</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1848_310978_1769000"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an Active Directory forest, a server that contains a writable copy of the Active Directory database, participates in Active Directory replication, and controls access to network resources.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="310978">DC</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769000">controlador de domini</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1848_47632_1769000"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an Active Directory forest, a server that contains a writable copy of the Active Directory database, participates in Active Directory replication, and controls access to network resources.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="47632">domain controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769000">controlador de domini</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18521_650875_2094974"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A whole number in the range 0 - 65,535 that corresponds to the Number property setting of the Err object. When combined with the Description property setting of the Err object, this number represents a particular error message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650875">error number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094974">número d'error</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18525_650879_2095060"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A text string that unambiguously refers to a hardware or software component under a certain context and can be used to access the data in that component.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650879">identifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095060">identificador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18529_650883_1098314"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Data that is stored outside of the application that is currently in use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650883">external data</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098314">dades externes</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18538_650892_2094784"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The part of PivotTable or PivotChart view that contains filter fields.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650892">filter area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094784">àrea de filtre</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18539_650893_1098315"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field in the filter area that you can use to filter data displayed in PivotTable or PivotChart view. Filter fields perform the same functions as page fields in Microsoft Excel PivotTable reports.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650893">filter field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098315">camp de filtre</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18548_650902_2094986"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Able to move freely as its own window. A floating window is always on top. Toolbars, menu bars, the toolbox, and palettes can float.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650902">floating</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094986">flotant</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1855_307383_1545836"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of validating software with the manufacturer. Activation confirms the genuine status of a product and that the product key has not been compromised. It establishes a relationship between the software’s product key and a particular installation of that software on a device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307383">activation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545836">activació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1856_52994_2997994"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Expressed as n! (n factorial), the result of multiplying the successive integers from 1 through n; n! equals n x (n - 1) x (n - 2) x ... x 1.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="52994">factorial</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2997994">factorial</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18560_650914_2094792"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The faint vertical and horizontal lines that appear in the drawing window when the grid is turned on. You can use grid lines to help position shapes precisely.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650914">grid lines</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094792">línies de quadrícula</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18568_650922_2095057"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type for an Access database field that stores hyperlink addresses. An address can have up to four parts and is written using the following format: A data type for an Access database field that stores hyperlink addresses. An address can have up to four parts and is written using the following format: displaytext#address#subaddress#.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650922">Hyperlink data type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095057">tipus de dades de l'enllaç</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18577_650931_2095065"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A driver you can specify that allows access to external database formats such as dBASE, Excel, and Paradox. The Microsoft Access database engine installs (loads) these ISAM drivers when referenced by your application.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650931">installable ISAM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095065">ISAM instal·lable</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18585_650939_2094796"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A line that connects fields between two tables and shows how the data is related. The type of join indicates which records are selected for the query's result set.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650939">join line</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094796">línia d'unió</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18590_650944_1545794"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Resolving resource conflicts or overallocations by delaying or splitting certain tasks. When Project levels a resource, its selected assignments are distributed and rescheduled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650944">leveling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545794">anivellament</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18598_650952_2095074"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character, usually a comma or semicolon, that separates elements in a list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650952">list-separator character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095074">caràcter de separació de llista</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="186_3712_761257"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To change to a newer, and/or more powerful or sophisticated version of a product.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3712">upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="761257">actualitzar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18609_650963_2095087"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A macro containing AddMenu actions that you can use to create a custom menu bar or shortcut menu.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650963">menu bar macro</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095087">macro de barra de menús</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1861_44576_1275942"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of distributing and installing a software program throughout an entire organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44576">deployment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1275942">implementació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1861_592529_1275942"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of distributing and installing a software program throughout an entire organization.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592529">software deployment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1275942">implementació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18613_650967_2095093"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An editor that is used to add text, edit HTML tags, and edit any Microsoft Visual Basic Scripting Edition (VBScript) code in a data access page. You can also view your page in the Script Editor as it would appear in a Web browser.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650967">Microsoft Script Editor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095093">Microsoft Script Editor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18616_650970_2095097"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The mode in which you can move columns in Datasheet view by using the left and right arrow keys.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650970">Move mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095097">mode de desplaçament</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1862_380991_2392097"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of Web sites that have the same owner and share administration settings. Each site collection contains a top-level site, can contain one or more subsites, and may have a shared navigation structure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="380991">site collection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2392097">col·lecció de llocs</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1864_558511_567946"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An incoming conversation that was not acknowledged by the user. Missed conversation notifications are saved and reported to the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="558511">missed conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="567946">conversa perduda</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1870_1413160_2714499"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that fits conveniently on a desk or table, and is not designed to be portable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1413160">desktop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2714499">ordinador de taula</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1870_44821_2714499"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that fits conveniently on a desk or table, and is not designed to be portable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44821">desktop computer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2714499">ordinador de taula</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1881_68580_1555459"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that enables a program to work with the user (the user interface, which can be a command-line interface, menu-driven, or a graphical user interface), with another program such as the operating system, or with the computer's hardware.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="68580">interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1555459">interfície</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18827_651178_2095100"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that automatically corrects common side effects that occur when you rename forms, reports, tables, queries, fields, or controls on forms and reports. However, Name AutoCorrect cannot repair all references to renamed objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651178">Name AutoCorrect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095100">correcció automàtica de noms</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18829_651180_2095101"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A button that is used to move through records or through the pages of a document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651180">navigation button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095101">botó de navegació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18834_651185_2095107"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fundamental data type representing any object that can be recognized by Visual Basic. Although you can declare any object variable as type Object, it is best to declare object variables according to their specific types.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651185">Object data type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095107">tipus de dades Objecte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18839_651190_2095112"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A database for which an Open Database Connectivity (ODBC) driver that you can use for importing, linking to, or exporting data is supplied.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651190">ODBC database</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095112">base de dades ODBC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18843_651194_2095115"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field data type that you use for objects created in other applications that can be linked or embedded (inserted) in an Access database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651194">OLE Object data type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095115">tipus de dades Objecte OLE</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18858_651209_2095121"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The target destination for data that has been cut or copied by using a clipboard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651209">paste area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095121">àrea per enganxar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18868_651219_2095122"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of locking in which the page containing one or more records, including the record being edited, is unavailable to other users when you use the Edit method, and remains unavailable until you use the Update method.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651219">pessimistic locking</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095122">blocatge pessimista</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18871_651222_2095124"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An interactive table that summarizes large amounts of data by using format and calculation methods that you choose. You can rotate its row and column headings to view the data in different ways, similar to an Excel PivotTable report.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651222">PivotTable form</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095124">formulari de taula dinàmica</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18873_651224_1546355"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A schedule of task start and finish dates and resource and cost data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651224">plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546355">pla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18879_651230_2095129"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A variable that is declared within a procedure. Procedure-level variables are always private to the procedure in which they are declared.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651230">procedure-level variable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095129">variable de nivell de procediment</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18887_651238_1098363"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A resource with a pending resource allocation to a task assignment that has not yet been authorized. This resource assignment does not detract from the availability of the resource to work on other projects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651238">proposed resource</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098363">recurs proposat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18889_651240_2095130"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dynamic cross-reference of one or more table data fields (columns) that permits an ODBC table (server table) without a unique index to be edited.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651240">pseudo index</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095130">pseudoíndex</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18891_651242_1547587"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The degree of excellence, or the desired standards, in a product, process, or project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651242">quality</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1547587">qualitat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18895_651246_2095155"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A task that occurs repeatedly during the course of a project. For example, you might define the weekly status meeting as a recurring task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651246">recurring task</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095155">tasca periòdica</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18900_651251_2095156"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The database to which the user has established a reference from the current database. The user can create a reference to a database and then call procedures within standard modules in that database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651251">referenced database</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095156">base de dades referida</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18906_651257_2095160"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To redraw the screen. The Repaint method completes any pending screen updates for a specified form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651257">repaint</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095160">tornar a dibuixar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18908_651259_2095165"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Excel template (.xlt file) that includes one or more queries or PivotTable reports that are based on external data. When you save a report template, Excel saves the query definition but doesn't store the queried data in the template.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651259">report template</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095165">plantilla d'informe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18913_651264_1098373"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of resources that is available for assignment to project tasks. A resource pool can be used exclusively by one project or can be shared by several projects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651264">resource pool</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098373">conjunt de recursos</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18915_651266_1098374"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An account of how many hours a resource is scheduled to work within a given time period, and thus an indicator of resources allocation within that time period.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651266">resource usage</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098374">ús dels recursos</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18922_651273_1098276"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A template that can be used as a project and task calendar to specify default working and nonworking time for a set of resources.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651273">base calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098276">calendari base</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18926_651277_1546103"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A representation of the communication path between actors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651277">binding</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546103">vinculació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18928_651279_2095153"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small box or bar to the left of a record that you can click to select the entire record in Datasheet view and Form view.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651279">record selector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095153">selector del registre</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18936_651287_2631566"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A business application that provides private, customizable websites that allow users to collaborate on projects and documents anyone to whom you grant permission.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651287">workspace</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2631566">àrea de treball</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18939_651290_2392067"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A customizable landing page for a business application or workspace that uses Web Parts to display selected information. It can provide a comprehensive look at the information inside the application or workspace by consolidating lists, libraries, text, images and other data into a dynamic, customizable information portal.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651290">dashboard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2392067">escriptori digital</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1894_234827_1547524"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Windows that checks for problems associated with network connections.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="234827">Diagnostics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1547524">Diagnòstic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1894_237891_1547524"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Windows that checks for problems associated with network connections.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237891">Windows Diagnostics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1547524">Diagnòstic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18941_651347_1546361"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An actor's interface component through which actors communicate with other actors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651347">port</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546361">port</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18942_651778_1547480"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any one-dimensional (1-D) shape that can be glued between two shapes in a drawing to connect the shapes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651778">connector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1547480">connector</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1895_186189_364183"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One of the presets for 3D rotation effects. When selected, specifies that the object will be rotated off-axis.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="186189">off-axis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="364183">fora de l'eix</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1898_67709_2052574"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To load the program and installation files onto your computer or device so that the program runs correctly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="67709">install</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2052574">instal·lar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1898_67709_722471"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To load the program and installation files onto your computer or device so that the program runs correctly.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="67709">install</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="722471">instal·la-ho ara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1901_92735_1546353"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A symbolic value used in place of a real value that is unknown or unavailable at the current time, or that is not displayed for security reasons.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="92735">placeholder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546353">marcador de posició</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1901_92735_2145183"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A symbolic value used in place of a real value that is unknown or unavailable at the current time, or that is not displayed for security reasons.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="92735">placeholder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2145183">contenidor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1902_57264_1555375"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Capable of using or being displayed on the full area of a display screen. Applications running in windowing environments, although they might use the entire area of the screen, commonly allocate different areas to different windows, any of which can be enlarged to fill the entire screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="57264">full screen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="155