tual disk to the user, backed by a file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1080693">attach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1545906">exposar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21965_782196_1359765"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that works with data in groups of 32 bits at a time. The Apple Macintosh II and higher models are 32-bit machines, in terms of both the word size of their microprocessors and the size of the data buses, as are computers based on the Intel 80386 and higher-level microprocessors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782196">32-bit machine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1359765">ordinador de 32 bits</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21965_782197_1359765"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that works with data in groups of 32 bits at a time. The Apple Macintosh II and higher models are 32-bit machines, in terms of both the word size of their microprocessors and the size of the data buses, as are computers based on the Intel 80386 and higher-level microprocessors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782197">32 bit machine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1359765">ordinador de 32 bits</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21990_782330_1547605"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To uninstall all software on a computer and reinstall a new Windows image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782330">re-image</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1547605">tornar a crear la imatge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21996_782344_1546094"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small pop-up window that informs users of a non-critical problem or special condition in a control.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782344">balloon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546094">globus</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="220_31883_2094760"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A module that can contain the definition for a new object where each instance of a class creates a new object and procedures defined in the module become properties and methods of the object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="31883">class module</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2094760">mòdul de classe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22015_782379_2627513"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer (usually quite powerful) that is used solely as a network server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782379">dedicated server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2627513">servidor especialitzat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22019_782423_2482503"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An entry in a list, catalog, or directory providing information about a Web site, product or item for sale, or service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782423">listing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2482503">fitxa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22021_782458_2520709"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device used on communications circuits that decreases distortion by amplifying or regenerating a signal so that it can be transmitted onward in its original strength and form. On a network, a repeater connects two networks or two network segments at the physical layer of the ISO/OSI reference model and regenerates the signal.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782458">repeater</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2520709">repetidor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22039_782585_2913426"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that collects biometric data for a variety of applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782585">biometric sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2913426">sensor biomètric</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22040_782586_1769094"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A sensor that uses ultrasound, infrared, heat or vibration stimuli to detect movement.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782586">motion sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769094">sensor de moviment</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22041_782588_1770088"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A biometric sensor that analyses your eye retina to recognize or authenticate identity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782588">retinal scanner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770088">escàner de retina</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22042_782589_1769010"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that can respond to an applied stimulus by generating an electrical signal.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782589">electrical sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769010">sensor elèctric</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22043_782590_1769087"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that is used for mechanical measurement of force, scale, pressure, strain, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782590">mechanical sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769087">sensor mecànic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22044_782669_1769016"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that tracks environmental changes such as temperature, atmospheric pressure, humidity, wind speed and wind direction.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782669">environmental sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769016">sensor ambiental</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22045_782671_1770077"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of sensor that can determine without physical contact if an object/person is nearby, or can be used to measure the distance between the object/person and the sensor device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782671">proximity sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770077">sensor de proximitat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22047_1053912_1770089"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of sensor (such as a proximity sensor) that uses radio frequency identification (RFID) for a numerous purposes, such as identification of physical items, automatic log on, location of people, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1053912">radio frequency identification sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770089">sensor RFID</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22047_782676_1770089"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of sensor (such as a proximity sensor) that uses radio frequency identification (RFID) for a numerous purposes, such as identification of physical items, automatic log on, location of people, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782676">RFID sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770089">sensor RFID</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22048_782677_1769063"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A sensor that responds to a pre-defined amount of light.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782677">light sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769063">fotosensor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2205_269322_1097537"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Classified or identified according to color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269322">color-coded</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097537">codificat amb colors</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22050_1700972_1816966"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Internet site that provides a collection of products and services developed by Microsoft partners for Microsoft Office users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1700972">Downloads Marketplace</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1816966">Botiga de l'Office</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22050_1700974_1816966"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Internet site that provides a collection of products and services developed by Microsoft partners for Microsoft Office users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1700974">Office Store</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1816966">Botiga de l'Office</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22050_782680_1816966"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Internet site that provides a collection of products and services developed by Microsoft partners for Microsoft Office users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="782680">Office Marketplace</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1816966">Botiga de l'Office</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22080_783138_2079096"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To remove a Bluetooth link or connection between two Bluetooth–enabled devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="783138">unpair</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2079096">desaparellar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22085_783181_2520701"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A circuit that alternates between two possible states when a pulse is received at the input. For example, if the output of a flip-flop is high and a pulse is received at the input, the output "flips" to low; a second input pulse "flops" the output back to high, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="783181">flip-flop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2520701">flip-flop</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22085_783216_2520701"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A circuit that alternates between two possible states when a pulse is received at the input. For example, if the output of a flip-flop is high and a pulse is received at the input, the output "flips" to low; a second input pulse "flops" the output back to high, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="783216">bistable multivibrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2520701">flip-flop</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22087_783218_2520703"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A circuit element that burns out or breaks when the current passing through it exceeds a certain level. A fuse protects a circuit from damage caused by excess current. It performs the same function as a circuit breaker, but it cannot be reset, so it must be replaced if it breaks. A fuse consists of a short length of wire of a specific composition and thickness; the thicker the wire, the more current it can pass before the wire melts and breaks the circuit.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="783218">fuse</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2520703">fusible</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2209_95057_1375828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user's right to perform a specific task, usually one that affects an entire computer system rather than a particular object. Privileges are assigned by administrators to individual users or groups of users as part of the security settings for the computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="95057">privilege</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1375828">privilegi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22135_784819_2016442"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view mode in Internet Explorer that determines whether content is rendered as if users were viewing it in a previous version of Internet Explorer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="784819">Compatibility View</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2016442">Visualització de compatibilitat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2215_295551_722506"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A report containing news or information, can be printed or distributed electronically.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="295551">newsletter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="722506">butlletí d'informació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2216_143575_2735667"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A discussion comment that is associated with a particular paragraph, image or table.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="143575">inline discussion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2735667">discussió incorporada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22169_1029910_2382238"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A new type of domain account designed to provide applications such as SQL Server or Exchange with automatic password management and simplified service principal name (SPN) management.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1029910">managed service account</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2382238">MSA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22169_2381365_2382238"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A new type of domain account designed to provide applications such as SQL Server or Exchange with automatic password management and simplified service principal name (SPN) management.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2381365">MSA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2382238">MSA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2218_210899_364089"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type that will provide support for storing binary files within an Access database. More similar to the SharePoint concept of attachments than the current OLE object fields in Access. The data will be stored as a raw blob within the database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210899">Attachment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="364089">Fitxer adjunt</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22183_1030868_2235204"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE) 802.11 wireless network in which Service Set Identifier (SSID) suppression is enabled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1030868">non-broadcast network</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2235204">xarxa oculta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22183_1030869_2235204"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE) 802.11 wireless network in which Service Set Identifier (SSID) suppression is enabled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1030869">hidden network</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2235204">xarxa oculta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22185_1030897_2279852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that prevents Internet Explorer from storing data about your browsing session. This helps prevent anyone else who might be using your computer from seeing where you visited and what you looked at on the Web.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1030897">InPrivate Browsing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2279852">Navegació de l'InPrivate</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22186_1081740_1953146"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that blocks third-party web content that could potentially track someone's web activity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1081740">InPrivate Filtering</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1953146">Protecció del seguiment</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22186_1509231_1953146"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that blocks third-party web content that could potentially track someone's web activity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1509231">Tracking Protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1953146">Protecció del seguiment</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22190_1031206_1963216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A form of IIS authentication in which IIS accepts client-certificates used to prove the client's identity. Using this form of authentication, IIS can optionally map a client certificate to a Windows user account by using an internal mapping table or Active Directory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1031206">certificate authentication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1963216">autenticació de certificats</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22202_1031390_1098391"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The position at which a particular item can be found: either an addressed location or a uniquely identified location on a disk, tape, or similar medium.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1031390">storage location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098391">ubicació d'emmagatzematge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22232_1032127_1097724"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An image and color combination designed to personalize a display window that is viewable to other people. For example, in Windows Live Messenger, someone can choose from a set of available scenes, or upload their own background image. They can also use a default color suggestion, or specify their own color. Someone's personalization is displayed in the main Messenger window (visible to themselves) and also in the main conversation window (visible to others).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032127">scene</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097724">escena</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22235_1032173_1097048"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The link group that includes links to the About Hotmail webpage, the What's New webpage, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032173">About</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097048">Quant a</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22237_1032194_1097899"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The API that defines a set of web services which can programmatically access the Windows Live Contacts Address Book database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032194">Windows Live Contacts API</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097899">API dels Contactes del Windows Live</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22238_1032196_1147616"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Live service for event planning and invitations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032196">Windows Live Events</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1147616">Trobades del Windows Live</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22239_1032199_1097901"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of Windows Live services optimized for use on mobile devices running Windows Mobile.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032199">Windows Live for Windows Mobile</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097901">Windows Live per a Windows Mobile</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22240_1032201_1097839"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Live webpage that displays security and safety-related activities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032201">Safety</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097839">Seguretat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22242_1032204_1097905"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The OneCare software designed to run on supported servers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032204">Windows Live OneCare for Server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097905">Windows Live OneCare for Server</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22243_1032209_1097888"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The link that appears above an incomplete content set and leads to the full list of items. For example, when a content module displays items 1–6, a "View all" link in line with the module label leads to a webpage that lists all items. The items that are available in preview are redundantly available in the list of all items, which may be paginated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1032209">View all</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097888">Visualitza-ho tot</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22244_1034315_1097850"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A favorite saved as a .url file in someone's "Shared favorites" folder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034315">shared favorite</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097850">preferit compartit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22245_1034323_1097353"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The image that appears in the conversation window.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034323">background</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097353">fons</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22246_1034324_1097585"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of feedback left by someone viewing content on a site.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034324">comment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097585">comentari</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22248_1034327_1769031"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer that belongs to a homegroup.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034327">homegroup computer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769031">ordinador del grup domèstic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22249_1034328_1769035"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A troubleshooter that helps find and fix problems with viewing computers or shared files in a homegroup.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034328">HomeGroup troubleshooter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769035">detector d'errors de Grup domèstic</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22259_1052661_1546547"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To group together multiple windows of the same application under a single button on the taskbar’s taskband.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1052661">combine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546547">combinar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22271_1034864_1098384"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows the user to digitally alter a picture to increase or decrease the sharpness of focus.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1034864">Sharpen and Soften</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098384">Ajustar la nitidesa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="223_321307_1769047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A signal sent by a device to get the attention of the processor when the device is ready to accept or send information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="321307">interrupt</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769047">interrupció</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="223_70091_1769047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A signal sent by a device to get the attention of the processor when the device is ready to accept or send information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="70091">interrupt request</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769047">interrupció</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="223_70092_1769047"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A signal sent by a device to get the attention of the processor when the device is ready to accept or send information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="70092">IRQ</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769047">interrupció</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22308_1040625_1769028"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software or device that helps control your home smart devices automatically.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1040625">home automation controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769028">controlador de domòtica</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22313_1040630_1768955"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An input device used chiefly for identification purposes that reads information that has been magnetically encoded, usually in two tracks, on a plastic card, such as a credit card or an employee badge.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1040630">card reader</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1768955">lector de targetes</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22317_1040657_1770100"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A notebook that is smaller in size and lighter in weight than a full-sized notebook, while retaining the same functionality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1040657">subnotebook</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca">