 record. When changes are made to a record type, those changes will affect all individual records of that type.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="182730">record type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1276056">tipus de registre</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2602_144805_2095095"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A variable that's declared in the Declarations section of a module by using the Private keyword. These variables are available to all procedures in the module.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144805">module-level variable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095095">variable de nivell de mòdul</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="26032_1260271_1359630"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Silverlight, an integrated set of types and methods that enable you to expose managed types to JavaScript and call JavaScript event handlers from managed types.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1260271">HTML Bridge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1359630">Pont HTML</term><termNote type=