he source can be a search service in the local server farm or another server farm, or another search engine that is compliant with the OpenSearch protocol.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1636440">result source</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1663888">origen de resultats</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29149_1506722_2303433"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A container for items that are deleted. Items in this container are visible to users with the appropriate permissions and to site collection administrators.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506722">first-stage Recycle Bin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2303433">Paperera de reciclatge de primer nivell</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29193_1644672_1663595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Web Part that renders named objects or named items in a workbook, such as tables, charts, slicers or a named range of cells.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1644672">named item view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1663595">visualització d'elements amb nom</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2923_59620_1769024"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of specifying software behavior by system administrators. Administrators set policies that are used to control how software features behave.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="59620">Group Policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1769024">Estratègia de grup</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29256_1506853_2303437"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A container for items that have been deleted from a first-stage Recycle Bin. Items in a second-stage Recycle Bin are visible only to site collection administrators.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506853">second-stage Recycle Bin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2303437">Paperera de reciclatge de segon nivell</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="29257_1506854_1586360"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A symmetric encryption key shared by two entities, such as between a user and the domain controller (DC), with a long lifetime. A password is a common example of a secret key. When used in a context that implies Kerberos only, a principal's secret key.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1506854">secret key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1586360">clau secreta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2927_184441_1381781"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option in the Options dialog box, on the Accounts tab. When the phone is integrated with Communicator, this option uses the automatic configuration settings for the phone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184441">Automatic configuration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1381781">Configuració automàtica</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2930_58202_1555379"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category for grouping or describing multimedia or games, such as music categorized as "classical" or "jazz".</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="58202">genre</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:l