rs to use ink to draw using their mouse, finger, or an inking tool, and whose ink resembles pencil graphite.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2432493">pencil</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434556">llapis</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42888_2432494_2434555"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool that allows users to use ink to draw using their mouse, finger, or an inking tool, and whose ink resembles traditional pen ink.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2432494">pen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434555">bolígraf</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42889_2432495_2434559"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A button that is activated when clicked once, and when clicked a second time, opens a menu that allows the user to modify the mode of the selected tool.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2432495">secondary action button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434559">botó d'accions secundàries</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42890_2432497_2434560"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A menu that is opened via a secondary action button and that gives users one or more options for changing the mode of the selected tool.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2432497">secondary action menu</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434560">menú d'accions secundàries</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42891_2432499_2434558"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An in-ribbon container that holds a collection of buttons and where the user can add additional buttons, reorganize buttons, and scroll through them when they are not all visible within the container.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2432499">scrollable button group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434558">grup de botons desplaçables</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42895_2433212_2434557"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The contextual ribbon tab that appears when users select a picture.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2433212">Picture</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434557">Imatge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42900_2433217_2435369"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Literally, "without stroke"; describes any typeface in which the characters have no serifs (the short lines or ornaments at the upper and lower ends of the strokes.) A sans serif typeface usually possesses a more straightforward, geometric appearance than a typeface with serifs and typically lacks the contrast between thick and thin strokes found in serif faces.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2433217">sans serif</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2435369">de pal sec</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4292_146988_2095128"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Describes any variables or constants declared within a procedure. Variables and constants declared within a procedure are available to that procedure only.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="146988">procedure level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2095128">nivell de procediment</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4293_37521_1546561"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The state of an expression or a variable (for example, when a result can be either true or false, or equal or not equal).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="37521">condition</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546561">condició</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42950_2434389_2437158"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Project view that displays each task and what resources have been assigned to it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434389">Task Usage</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2437158">Ús de tasques</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4296_309439_1137755"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A World Wide Web version of Windows Client Help.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="309439">Windows Assistance Online</term><termNote type="p