 portions by vertical or horizontal bars and having a separate function.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="90456">pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546272">subfinestra</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50777_2873906_2874194"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The interface in Microsoft Edge that allows users to customize their browser's appearance, privacy &amp; security options, and other configuration options.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2873906">Settings</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874194">Configuració</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50778_2873907_2874195"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The video camera capture mode for in which users can take slow-motion videos.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2873907">Slow-mo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874195">Càmera lenta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50779_2873908_2874196"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The information stream in MS Launcher relating to the user's work profile that contains information from their calendar, tasks to be completed, notes, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2873908">work feed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874196">canal de continguts de la feina</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50783_2874151_2886490"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The hostname from which a request was generated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874151">referrer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2886490">origen de referència</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27452_1768951"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27452">CAPI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1768951">CAPI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27453_1768951"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27453">CryptoAPI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1768951">CAPI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5085_27454_1768951"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An (API) that is provided as part of Microsoft Windows. CryptoAPI provides a set of functions that allow applications to encrypt or digitally sign data in a flexible manner while providing protection for the user's sensitive private key data. Actual cryptographic operations are performed by independent modules known as (CSPs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27454">Cryptography Application Programming Interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1768951">CAPI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50850_2874469_2875707"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app within Teams for Life in which users can securely store personal documents like passports or driver's licenses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874469">Safe</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2875707">Caixa forta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50852_2874471_2875913"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mechanism for Teams Rooms by which two or more accounts can be associated with a trust relationship to allows them to pull each other into meetings automatically, and coordinate which device will call, answer, provide audio/video, and participate in other meeting experiences.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874471">Coordinated Meetings</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2875913">Optimització de reunions</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50853_2874472_2875704"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The function in Teams for Educators by which teachers can return students' assignments to them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874472">return</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2875704">tornar les tasques</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50854_2874474_2875710"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An extension of Microsoft Graph to expand the types of content sources that are available in your Microsoft 365 productivity apps and the broader Microsoft ecosystem.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874474">Microsoft Graph content connector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2875710">connector de continguts del Microsoft Graph</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50855_2874475_2875701"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A SharePoint site with a personalized view of relevant knowledge across your organization on which users with permission can see topics and knowledge managers can manage topics.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874475">topic center</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">