m which can be used to host security solutions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929517">virtualization-based security</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929658">seguretat basada en virtualització</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52008_2929518_2929657"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows feature that uses hardware virtualization to create and isolate a secure region of memory from the normal operating system which can be used to host security solutions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929518">VBS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929657">VBS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52008_2929518_2929658"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows feature that uses hardware virtualization to create and isolate a secure region of memory from the normal operating system which can be used to host security solutions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929518">VBS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929658">seguretat basada en virtualització</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52010_2929644_2929779"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To respond to an invitation and indicate whether or not you plan to attend the event that the invitation is for.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929644">RSVP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929779">RSUP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52029_2929967_2930200"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A computer security mechanism that consists of a second stack that “shadows” the call stack to enforce integrity on return addresses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2929967">shadow stack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2930200">pila paral·lela</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5203_120859_1537136"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Data that consists of characters representing the words and symbols of human speech.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120859">text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammatica