ures that enables premium capabilities for additional meeting scenarios, including Virtual appointments and webinars.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093360">Teams Premium</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093510">Microsoft Teams Premium</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54253_3093360_3093511"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The paid Microsoft Teams offer with additional features that enables premium capabilities for additional meeting scenarios, including Virtual appointments and webinars.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093360">Teams Premium</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093511">Teams Premium</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54254_3093361_3093512"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The website where Microsoft shares security engineering practices that are used to build and operate highly secure apps and services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093361">Security Engineering Portal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093512">Portal d'enginyeria de seguretat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54255_3093362_3093506"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The worldwide team of cybersecurity experts operating in most countries, across all organizations (public and private), with expertise to secure an environment post-security breach and to help users prevent a breach in the first place.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093362">Compromise Recovery Security Practice</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093506">Equip de seguretat per a la recuperació de vulneracions</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54255_3093362_3093507"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The worldwide team of cybersecurity experts operating in most countries, across all organizations (public and private), with expertise to secure an environment post-security breach and to help users prevent a breach in the first place.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093362">Compromise Recovery Security Practice</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093507">CRSP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54255_3093363_3093506"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The worldwide team of cybersecurity experts operating in most countries, across all organizations (public and private), with expertise to secure an environment post-security breach and to help users prevent a breach in the first place.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093363">CRSP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093506">Equip de seguretat per a la recuperació de vulneracions</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54255_3093363_3093507"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The worldwide team of cybersecurity experts operating in most countries, across all organizations (public and private), with expertise to secure an environment post-security breach and to help users prevent a breach in the first place.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093363">CRSP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3093507">CRSP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54265_3094167_3094713"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Microsoft's official video series for IT Pros, Solution Architects, Developers, and Tech Enthusiasts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094167">Microsoft Mechanics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094713">Microsoft Mechanics</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54266_3094170_3094714"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The online page under Microsoft Security website where users can learn about a variety of cybersecurity, identity, and compliance topics and best practices at Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094170">Security 101</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094714">Nocions bàsiques sobre seguretat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54267_3094172_3094712"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows utility that checks which files are in use and by which processes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094172">File Locksmith</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094712">Serraller de fitxers</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54268_3094353_3094398"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A role assigned to experienced Power Apps makers to help others. The advisor will show as someone that can be contacted for help in the Power Apps Virtual Agent chat.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094353">advisor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094398">assessor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54269_3094354_3094399"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A micro-app that uses enterprise data that can be sent as content in Teams.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094354">card</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094399">targeta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54270_3094355_3094400"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Power Platform offering that enables you to deploy your small independent apps (mini-apps) into Teams chats, Microsoft Outlook emails, web chat, or third-party apps. Customers deploying new or updated business workflows enjoy increased efficiency and uptake by deploying apps in popular products such as Teams, as opposed to deploying entirely new sites or apps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094355">Cards</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094400">Targetes</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54271_3094356_3094401"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that allows app makers to add collaboration features (meetings, tasks, approvals, etc.) into apps built with Power Apps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094356">Collaboration controls</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094401">Controls de col·laboració</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54272_3094357_3094402"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Dataverse security configuration setting that allows users to manage the permission of users and teams to read, create, or write in secured columns. For example, the System Administrator column security profile gives full access to all secured columns.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094357">column security profile</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094402">perfil de seguretat de la columna</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54273_3094358_3094403"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An extra layer of security that helps detect and mitigate some types of web attacks such as data theft, site defacement, or the distribution of malware.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094358">content security policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094403">norma de seguretat del contingut</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54274_3094359_3094404"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A special type of URI that encodes the actual resource content, instead of just pointing to it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094359">data URI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094404">URI de dades</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54275_3094360_3094405"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A pipeline that eliminates much of today's application lifecycle management (ALM) complexity by bringing ALM automation into the product and making it accessible to all makers, admins, and developers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094360">deployment pipeline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094405">pipeline d'implementació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54276_3094361_3094406"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An environment to build and test with Power Apps, Power Automate, and Microsoft Dataverse. It can be created by users who have the Power Apps Developer Plan.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094361">developer environment</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094406">entorn de desenvolupador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54277_3094362_3094407"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Power Apps feature that accelerates the getting started process by taking existing content (e.g., a picture of your paper form, a screenshot of a design you like, a PPT, a PDF, or a Figma design file) and converting them into a working Power App with UI and data without requiring the maker to learn how to build an app.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094362">express design</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094407">disseny exprés</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54278_3094363_3094408"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of governance capabilities, found in the Power Platform Admin Center that will simplify, automate, and streamline IT administration of the Power Platform.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094363">Managed Environments</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094408">Entorns administrats</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54279_3094364_3094409"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The annual event sponsored by Microsoft dedicated to Microsoft Power Platform products including Power Apps, Power Automate, Power BI, Power Pages, and Power Virtual Agents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094364">Power Platform Conference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094409">Conferència sobre el Power Platform</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54280_3094365_3094410"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Power Apps connector available to Premium License Plan subscribers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094365">premium connector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094410">connector prèmium</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54281_3094366_3094411"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Power Platform feature that shows how much finance and operations storage your organization is using compared with how much its license entitles it to.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094366">storage capacity reporting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094411">informes sobre la capacitat d'emmagatzematge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54282_3094367_3094412"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type in Power Fx that can hold any data structure, complex or simple. It can't be used directly and requires explicit conversion to a data type. Fields in records in an untyped object can be accessed using the dot notation, and existence of fields is only verified at runtime.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094367">untyped object</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3094412">objecte sense tipus</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54283_3095195_3095479"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The protection of data in use by performing computation in a hardware-based Trusted Execution Environment.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3095195">confidential computing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3095479">informàtica confidencial</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54285_3095197_3095483"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The free global learning event on Data, Analytics and AI for data professionals that features a keynote session and more than 200 breakout sessions delivered by Azure Data engineering, partner organizations, and community leaders.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3095197">Data Platform Virtual Summit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3095483">Data Platform Virtual Summit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNot