d other business data, and perform new types of computations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3115363">plugin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3117547">connector</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5487_26569_1546153"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Broadly, any device that performs arithmetic operations on numbers. Sophisticated calculators can be programmed for certain functions and can store values in memory, but they differ from computers in several ways: they have a fixed set of commands, they do not recognize text, they cannot retrieve values stored in a data file, and they cannot find and use values generated by a program such as a spreadsheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26569">calculator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1546153">calculadora</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54958_3116446_3116933"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The geographically defined boundary consisting of the countries in the European Union (EU) and the European Free Trade Association (EFTA) within which Microsoft has committed to store and process customer data for its major commercial enterprise online services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3116446">EU Data Boundary</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3116933">Frontera de dades de la UE</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54959_3116447_3116929"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To instruct, train, or guide.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3116447">coach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3116929">assessorar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54960_3116448_3116930"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An individual who gives instructions, training, or guidance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3116448">coach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3116930">assessor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54961_3116449_3116934"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft Teams feature that allows users to discuss content that'